    <text>
    <body>
        
        <div type="letter">
            <div type="text">
                <opener>
                    <placeName>Down Farnborough Kent</placeName>
                    <date>Saturday</date>
                    <salute>My dear Hooker</salute>
                </opener>
                <div type="transcription">
<p>I do not know whether this will find you at home, but if so &amp; you are disengaged, shall I come for a few hours talk on Friday Morning next, stomacho volente,— Send me one line by return of Post, which I apprehend I shall get on Tuesday Morning, or at latest on Wednesday before I start.—</p>
<p>I hope Sir William is better; if not, of course put me off.</p>
<p>Ever yours | C. Darwin</p> 
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>

        

        

        <div type="footnotes">
            <note xml:id="foot.f1">Dated from the reference to a proposed trip to London. On Saturday, 29 May, CD recorded the expenses of a trip to London in his Account Book (Down House MS). See also letters to J. D. Hooker, <ref target="./DCP-LETT-1091.xml" resp="#mjhawkins">[25 May 1847]</ref> and <ref target="./DCP-LETT-1092.xml" resp="#mjhawkins">[28 May 1847]</ref>.</note>
        </div>        
            
